  "response": "To configure the LLM and the embedding model globally in the current LlamaIndex, you need to utilize the `Settings` object, which was introduced to replace the older `ServiceContext` configuration. Here's how you can do it based on the provided context:\n\n1. **LLM Configuration:**\n   - The LLM can be configured by setting it in the `Settings` object. If you are not using OpenAI's default LLM, you will need to specify an alternative. For instance, if you want to use Ollama as your LLM, you can set it like this:\n\n     ```python\n     from llama_index.llms.ollama import Ollama\n\n     Settings.llm = Ollama()\n     ```\n\n2. **Embedding Model Configuration:**\n   - To set the embedding model globally, you will assign it to `Settings.embed_model`. If you do not specify this, LlamaIndex defaults to using `OpenAIEmbedding` with the `text-embedding-ada-002` model. To set a different model, such as a current OpenAI model or a local model, you can do the following:\n\n     - **For an OpenAI Model:**\n\n       ```python\n       from llama_index.embeddings.openai import OpenAIEmbedding\n\n       Settings.embed_model = OpenAIEmbedding(model=\"text-embedding-3-small\")\n       ```\n\n     - **For a HuggingFace Model:**\n\n       ```python\n       from llama_index.embeddings.huggingface import HuggingFaceEmbedding\n\n       Settings.embed_model = HuggingFaceEmbedding(model_name=\"BAAI/bge-base-en-v1.5\")\n       ```\n\nBy setting these configurations in the `Settings` object, you apply them as the default for every module in LlamaIndex. This approach ensures that the specified LLM and embedding model are used throughout your project, and they are only loaded when needed, optimizing resource usage.",
